<newsitem itemid="397522" id="root" date="1997-02-24" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Group Five half year earnings edge up.</title>
<headline>Group Five half year earnings edge up.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Dec 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     36.0	  vs 31.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 9.0	   vs 7.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   26.51	 vs 12.99</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   37.12	 vs 27.58</p>
<p>    Tax			 10.65	 vs 8.67</p>
<p>    Finance costs	   8.44	  vs 13.12</p>
<p>    Turnover		  1,197.96    vs 1,223.02</p>
<p>Full name: Group Five Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Construction firm Group Five Ltd said in a statement that all its divisions had contributed to profit growth except building and property development, where market conditions were difficult.  </p>
<p>Div payable April 7</p>
<p>on register March 20</p>
</text>
